    description: "Implement the ADR-0017 section 3a forward walk so the DDG actually adjudicates\nflows instead of labelling them.\n\nPREREQUISITES, all now known and each independently sufficient to keep it inert:\n  1. atomic_statement missing from cfg_nodes/{rust,typescript,java}.yaml, so\n     those extractors emit zero DDG edges (separate item).\n  2. cli.py gates propagation on the literal lang == \"python\".\n  3. Index DDG edges by symbol_id, not def_block (block ids are function-local).\n  4. TaintFlowFinding.confidence has no consumer -- verify_claims.py:853\n     hardcodes the string \"approximate\", and _flow_evidence_dict omits both\n     confidence and analysis_method entirely.\n\nSPEC GAP FOUND WHILE MEASURING: step 5 as written (\"if tainted data reaches a\nsink, record a finding\") must be implemented as \"a tainted variable is an\nARGUMENT AT THE SINK CALL SITE\". Implemented as \"a tainted def reaches the sink\nblock\" it kills almost nothing.\n\nPRE-REGISTERED EXPECTATION, from adjudicating the 9-repo cohort (192 distinct\nflows): roughly 13 percent fewer evidence rows and ZERO of 17 violated claim\nverdicts change. 69 percent of flows have source and sink in different\nfunctions, which intraprocedural DDG cannot connect by construction; a further\n26 of the 60 intraprocedural flows have no analyzable function at all (Django\nmigration pseudo-symbols with 0-0 spans, and JS taint attributed at file\ngranularity). Addressable domain is therefore about 18 percent of flows.\nIf a future measurement reports a much larger number, suspect the measurement.\n\nKNOWN TRADE TO OWN IN WRITING: without alias analysis (excluded by ADR-0017\nsection 7b) this introduces FALSE NEGATIVES on container/alias mutation. For a\nsecurity tool that is the expensive direction."  # c76f
    fields: {}  # c76f
- op: discuss  # 8493
  at: '2026-08-03T21:36:59Z'  # 8493
  by: agent  # 8493
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8493
  clock: 2  # 8493
  nonce: '8493'  # 8493
  message: "SECTION 3A IMPLEMENTED AND SHIPPED IN CONFIRM-ONLY MODE, PR #188 (dev\nb70f886306). Item stays todo_hard: the headline -- \"make the DDG forward walk\ndecide flow inclusion\" -- is not met, because refutation is unsound on the\ncurrent substrate.\n\nTHIS FILING LISTS FOUR PREREQUISITES, \"each independently sufficient to keep it\ninert\". There are SIX. The four filed are done or moot:\n  1. atomic_statement for rust/typescript/java -- rust+ts shipped (WI-tohuk);\n     java needs a def/use extractor first, filed separately.\n  2. cli.py gating on lang == \"python\" -- REMOVED.\n  3. index DDG edges by symbol_id, not def_block -- DONE.\n  4. TaintFlowFinding.confidence has no consumer -- still true, and it is the\n     next labelling phase; it does not block the walk.\n\nTHE TWO THAT ACTUALLY BLOCK IT, neither of them in the filing:\n\n  5. SECTION 4 FUNCTION SUMMARIES. Section 3a's own step 3 says \"At call sites,\n     apply function summaries (section 4)\". infer_summary and\n     load_function_summaries have ZERO production callers, and there is no\n     python or go catalogue at all -- the shipped summaries are rust_stdlib\n     and typescript_stdlib, i.e. the two languages that until this week had no\n     DDG, one of which has zero sinks. Without summaries, `fmt.Printf(cwd)`\n     (taint terminates) and `lst.append(x)` (taint escapes into the receiver)\n     are the same event: a use that defines nothing. So a \"no dependence\"\n     result cannot be distinguished from \"lost track of it\".\n\n  6. PER-CALL-SITE LINES. deduplicate_edges keeps the FIRST edge per\n     (src,dst,type) and discards the rest, so Edge.line is A call site, not\n     each one. caddy's printEnvironment calls fmt.Printf twelve times and the\n     graph records only line 454; the tainted call at 469 is invisible. Asking\n     \"does taint from 465 reach 454?\" answers a question about the wrong call\n     site. Fix shape is additive -- collect the dropped lines onto the\n     surviving edge as meta.call_lines -- rather than emitting N edges and\n     multiplying the call graph.\n\nPRE-REGISTRATION SCORED. Row volume: predicted ~13% fewer evidence rows,\nmeasured -10.3% on the unguarded arm. Close. Verdict changes: predicted ZERO,\nmeasured TWO -- and both were CORRECT removals (caddy ListenPacket->Chmod,\nwhere `address` is an INPUT to the source rather than its output; and\nListenUDP->tls.Client, where the sink is called 59 lines BEFORE the source).\nThe prediction missed them because it did not model single-flow claims: a\nverdict is a disjunction, so removing the one flow holding it flips it. That\nis the same structural fact that made WI-bifob flip two claims, and this\nestimate predates WI-bifob shipping.\n\nCONFIRM-ONLY IS MEASURABLY LIVE, not a no-op: caddy 5/169 findings (3.0%),\npretix 8/821 (1.0%) carry an earned precise label. Cohort A/B: 54 verdict\nrows, 311 flows, 270 displayed rows, 38 confirmed / 16 violated -- 0 cells\ndiffer, which is the contract for a confirm-only change.\n\nTRADE STILL OWNED IN WRITING, per this item's own note: once section 4 lands\nand refutation switches on, container/alias mutation becomes a false-negative\nsource. Section 7b excludes alias analysis by design, so the summaries must\ncarry mutates_self / param_to_self for the container APIs that actually appear\nat use-sites, or the same three-of-nine failure returns."  # 8493
- op: discuss  # a10e
  at: '2026-08-03T23:36:11Z'  # a10e
  by: agent  # a10e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a10e
  clock: 3  # a10e
  nonce: a10e  # a10e
  message: "PREREQUISITE 6 OF 6 IS DONE -- per-call-site lines. PR #190, merged as\n59321e8166.\n\nir.deduplicate_edges kept one edge per (src, dst, edge_type) and discarded\nevery call site's line but the first-encountered one. That model is correct\nfor a call graph and is unchanged; what was wrong is that no consumer could\nrecover the other sites. Section 4 needs them: deciding what a dataflow use at\nline U flows into requires knowing which callee is invoked at line U.\n\nThe survivor now carries meta.call_lines -- the sorted union of collapsed\nsites, its own line included, capped at 50. A single-site edge carries NO key,\nso absence reads as \"one site, and it is line\". apply_external_id_remap, which\nruns after dedup and collapses again once external dsts remap onto one\nboundary node, unions the same way it already unions referring_paths.\n\nMEASURED ON SELF-ANALYSIS, verified in both directions rather than counted:\n13,121 of 141,312 edges (9.29%) record more than one site -- median 2, p95 7,\n28 at the cap -- costing 0.22% of artifact size (411 KB of 186 MB). Positive\ncheck: every line recorded for catalog.py file -> _ts is a real _ts(...) call.\nNegative check: the UNRECORDED lines inside the same caller's span\n(cli.py 2559-2568) contain no .get( at all, so the field records call sites\nrather than every line in the caller.\n\nNOTHING CONSUMES IT YET, deliberately. taint.py still reads edge[\"line\"]\nalone. Shipping the retention on its own keeps its artifact-size and\ncorrectness effects readable instead of mixed into a section 4 behaviour\nchange. Wiring it into propagate_taint_ddg is the first step of the next PR\nand gets its own A/B, because feeding the existing section 3a guards\n(source_tracked, sink_after_source) more call sites can only ADD\nconfirmations -- a change worth measuring separately from section 4 itself.\n\nORDER REVISED. My earlier note here said catalogue-then-wire. Reading the\nsection 4 loader changed that: enumerating precisely which callees appear at\ntaint use-sites requires the walk to consult them, so the enumeration is a\nBYPRODUCT of the wiring rather than a prerequisite for it. Guessing the set\nfrom a superset (every callee of every taint-carrying function) would be both\nlarger and less accurate. Revised: (1) call_lines [done], (2) wire section 4\nwith uncatalogued -> escaped plus a measurement mode, (3) cohort run yields\nthe enumerated set, (4) author python_stdlib.yaml + go_stdlib.yaml covering\nit, (5) cohort run for coverage and effect, at which point refutation is\nsound.\n\nAND A CORRECTION TO MY OWN EARLIER REASONING. I recorded that an uncatalogued\ncallee \"reads as escaped\" because get_default_summary is conservative. It does\nnot. get_default_summary returns param_to_return = {0..9: True} -- everything\npropagates. So wiring section 4 with an empty catalogue would fail the other\nway: every callee assumed to pass taint through, no branch ever closes, no\nFalse ever earned, removal still blocked, and confirmation MORE eager and thus\nless trustworthy. The conclusion (catalogue is load-bearing) is unchanged; the\nmechanism I had written for it was wrong.\n\nDesign decision that follows: get_default_summary will NOT be used on this\npath. Uncatalogued callees route to escaped, which is exactly today's\nbehaviour -- so 0% catalogue coverage reproduces today's output byte for byte,\nand every behaviour change is attributable to a catalogue entry somebody\nwrote. The catalogue becomes load-bearing by construction rather than by\ndiscipline."  # a10e
